<%# Every key the writing room answers to, in the order a writer meets them: the marks he
    makes inside a sentence, the shape he gives a block, then the room itself. Opened with
    ⌘/ or from the foot of the settings panel. The wording matches the toolbar's own
    titles — "Bold (⌘B)" there, ⌘B · Bold here — because they are the same fact said
    twice, and an integration test holds the two together.

    A real <dialog>: the browser traps Tab inside it, closes it on Escape and hands focus
    back to whatever opened it, so none of that is written here. It sits outside the
    autosaving form on purpose — the sheet is chrome, and nothing in it is the post. %>
<dialog class="shortcut-sheet" data-editor-target="shortcuts"
        data-action="click->editor#closeShortcutsOnBackdrop">
  <header class="shortcut-sheet__head">
    <h2>Keyboard shortcuts</h2>
    <button type="button" class="panel-close" data-action="editor#closeShortcuts" aria-label="Close shortcuts">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m4 4 8 8M12 4l-8 8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
    </button>
  </header>

  <table class="shortcut-sheet__table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Keys</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><kbd>⌘B</kbd></td><td>Bold</td></tr>
      <tr><td><kbd>⌘I</kbd></td><td>Italic</td></tr>
      <tr><td><kbd>⌘⇧X</kbd></td><td>Strikethrough</td></tr>
      <tr><td><kbd>⌘E</kbd></td><td>Inline code</td></tr>
      <tr><td><kbd>⌘K</kbd></td><td>Link</td></tr>
      <tr><td><kbd>⌘⌥2</kbd></td><td>Heading 2</td></tr>
      <tr><td><kbd>⌘⌥3</kbd></td><td>Heading 3</td></tr>
      <tr><td><kbd>⌘⌥4</kbd></td><td>Heading 4</td></tr>
      <tr><td><kbd>⌘⌥0</kbd></td><td>Paragraph</td></tr>
      <tr><td><kbd>⌘S</kbd></td><td>Save now — the editor saves on its own every couple of seconds</td></tr>
      <tr><td><kbd>⌘P</kbd></td><td>Open the reader's view in a new tab</td></tr>
      <tr><td><kbd>⌘⇧P</kbd></td><td>Publishing</td></tr>
      <tr><td><kbd>⌘/</kbd></td><td>This sheet</td></tr>
      <tr><td><kbd>Esc</kbd></td><td>Close whatever is open</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p class="shortcut-sheet__foot">On Windows and Linux, press Ctrl wherever this says ⌘.</p>
</dialog>
